   "isFreePreview": true,
   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">BDF201 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 14477 · Decision 1028/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 21/08/2026 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">BDF201 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 14477 · QĐ 1028/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 21/08/2026 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>Students must attend at least 80% of contact sessions to be eligible for the final assessment. - Complete required readings and pre-class preparation; actively participate in discussions, case analyses, and in-class exercises. Complete and submit all quizzes/assignments/labs/projects on time; contribute fairly and professionally in group work. Follow academic integrity rules (no plagiarism, proper citation, no unauthorized collaboration); use AI tools responsibly and transparently when allowed by the instructor. - Use laptops/tablets in class strictly for learning activities. For hands-on blockchain labs: use testnets/sandbox accounts unless explicitly instructed; do NOT share private keys/seed phrases; follow security best practices.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>Students must attend at least 80% of contact sessions to be eligible for the final assessment. - Complete required readings and pre-class preparation; actively participate in discussions, case analyses, and in-class exercises. Complete and submit all quizzes/assignments/labs/projects on time; contribute fairly and professionally in group work. Follow academic integrity rules (no plagiarism, proper citation, no unauthorized collaboration); use AI tools responsibly and transparently when allowed by the instructor. - Use laptops/tablets in class strictly for learning activities. For hands-on blockchain labs: use testnets/sandbox accounts unless explicitly instructed; do NOT share private keys/seed phrases; follow security best practices.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions (8)</h3>\n<p>Questions the syllabus asks you to think through before or during the session — try answering them yourself first.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo (8)</h3>\n<p>Câu hỏi syllabus yêu cầu bạn suy nghĩ trước/trong buổi học — tự trả lời trước khi xem bài.</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Code<br><small>Mã</small></th><th>Question (verbatim)<br><small>Câu hỏi (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td>CQ1</td><td>Why isn’t blockchain “just an Excel database”? Identify which properties are essential for DeFi, and justify with one concrete DeFi use case.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td>CQ2</td><td>In a trustless setting (no bank), how can a digital payment system prevent double spending?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td>CQ1</td><td>A single transaction in a block is modified. Why does this matter for scalability and light verification?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td>CQ1</td><td>Two miners produce two valid blocks at the same height. Explain how a P2P network resolves this fork. What does “finality” mean for DeFi trades and liquidations?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td>CQ1</td><td>Miners/validators spend resources to secure the network. Using incentives, explain why honest behavior can be rational. Under what conditions could attacks become more feasible?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td>CQ2</td><td>During congestion, how are transactions selected from the mempool (fees, size, waiting time, validity)?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td>CQ3</td><td>What are the impacts on DeFi protocols (DEX swaps, lending, collateral liquidations)? Suggest practical risk mitigations.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td>CQ4</td><td>A user signs the wrong transaction or approves a malicious smart contract. Why is it hard to reverse on-chain?</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14477\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14477</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14477\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14477</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
